WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.790 --> 00:00:03.540
(sirens blaring)

00:00:17.939 --> 00:00:19.740
- [Mark] All right, Juicy Fruit.

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:22.390
Juicy Fruit, where'd you
grow up? Where are you from?

00:00:23.230 --> 00:00:24.710
- [Juicy Fruit] Watts, California.

00:00:24.710 --> 00:00:25.990
- [Mark] And tell me about your family.

00:00:25.990 --> 00:00:28.310
You had both your parents
when you were a kid?

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:29.163
- [Juicy Fruit] No.

00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:32.080
- [Mark] Who raised you?

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:36.110
- Well, I was in and out of
foster care and group homes.

00:00:36.110 --> 00:00:37.463
- [Mark] Where was mom and dad?

00:00:38.769 --> 00:00:40.660
- I really don't know.

00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:43.123
I only seen my mother so often, so.

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:47.100
But my mother was an alcoholic,

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:48.960
my dad was too busy running the streets

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:50.363
gang banger and everything.

00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:55.320
- [Mark] And how was your childhood?

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:56.270
- Pretty messed up.

00:00:58.978 --> 00:01:01.978
- [Mark] What kind of stuff went on?

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:05.823
- Shit, I got raped for like 10 years.

00:01:07.240 --> 00:01:08.740
- [Mark] In the foster system?

00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:10.853
By who?

00:01:11.810 --> 00:01:14.693
- By one of the guys that
actually worked in the house.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:21.233
- [Mark] Did you say anything to anyone?

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:25.700
- I tried, nobody really
believed me about it.

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:29.000
But what could I do?

00:01:40.272 --> 00:01:42.272
(sighs)

00:01:47.393 --> 00:01:52.343
Well I just went around from
foster homes, group homes and

00:01:56.910 --> 00:01:59.090
had somebody set my bed on fire

00:02:01.161 --> 00:02:03.061
while I was in it, while I was asleep.

00:02:07.250 --> 00:02:08.083
- [Mark] I'm sorry?

00:02:08.083 --> 00:02:09.517
- While I was asleep at the, what was it?

00:02:09.517 --> 00:02:11.823
The group because yeah, the group home.

00:02:14.846 --> 00:02:17.429
(sighs deeply)

00:02:19.230 --> 00:02:20.940
I hate talking about this.

00:02:26.890 --> 00:02:28.743
- [Mark] If you'd rather not, it's okay.

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:33.160
I'll pay you either way.

00:02:37.150 --> 00:02:38.503
- No, I'll finish.

00:02:44.920 --> 00:02:46.840
What's the next question?

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:50.260
- [Mark] So you're molested for
10 years in the foster home,

00:02:50.260 --> 00:02:51.903
was there any other abuse?

00:02:55.340 --> 00:02:58.270
- Well, basically with
this guy that used to come,

00:02:58.270 --> 00:03:00.100
they had a day shift,

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:02.213
a evening shift, and he had a night shift.

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:09.260
This one guy will come in
my room and come get me.

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:11.210
Basically, he'd chain me up like a dog.

00:03:26.793 --> 00:03:28.793
(sighs)

00:03:30.240 --> 00:03:31.790
- [Mark] This started what age?

00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:36.597
- When I was like, what? 12, 13?

00:03:43.662 --> 00:03:46.245
(sighs deeply)

00:03:47.407 --> 00:03:50.407
- [Mark] I'm sorry, so you went
out on your own at what age?

00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:55.540
- Well, off and on, I
was on my own basically

00:03:55.540 --> 00:03:59.680
from the time I was
about, what? 10 till...

00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:03.570
Shit, till time I turned 18.

00:04:03.570 --> 00:04:06.310
I was off and on in between
group homes, on the street,

00:04:06.310 --> 00:04:08.683
foster homes, in and out of jail.

00:04:16.041 --> 00:04:17.710
- [Mark] And you started
working as a prostitute

00:04:17.710 --> 00:04:18.543
at what age?

00:04:20.539 --> 00:04:25.539
- 12.

00:04:27.518 --> 00:04:28.518
- [Mark] 12.

00:04:29.670 --> 00:04:32.780
Were you doing that on
your own or with a pimp?

00:04:32.780 --> 00:04:33.877
- Yeah, I had a pimp.

00:04:38.860 --> 00:04:40.372
Yeah, I had my daughter, what?

00:04:40.372 --> 00:04:42.933
Right before I turned 18.

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:46.300
I was still out there making money.

00:04:54.203 --> 00:04:57.770
I almost lost her to the
system because my mom...

00:04:57.770 --> 00:05:00.490
Basically after making contact with her,

00:05:00.490 --> 00:05:03.790
my mom tried to take my
daughter away from me

00:05:06.114 --> 00:05:08.550
'cause she tried to say I was on,

00:05:08.550 --> 00:05:10.520
basically on drugs and everything.

00:05:10.520 --> 00:05:13.663
Like, I might smoke weed
but that's about it.

00:05:19.210 --> 00:05:20.850
I went through court back and forth

00:05:20.850 --> 00:05:22.150
with that for a long time.

00:05:24.680 --> 00:05:27.030
And then I had my son

00:05:29.770 --> 00:05:31.853
when I was, what? About turned 22.

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:37.803
Still working the streets.

00:05:42.430 --> 00:05:46.663
I almost lost my son when I
was pregnant, turning date.

00:05:48.326 --> 00:05:49.210
- [Mark] What happened?

00:05:49.210 --> 00:05:51.223
Dude sucked me on my stomach so hard.

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:56.623
After he got finished handling business,

00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:02.773
he took the money back,

00:06:05.990 --> 00:06:08.643
basically, and he just left me there.

00:06:18.650 --> 00:06:20.383
I was seven and a half months.

00:06:23.460 --> 00:06:26.483
So they ended up having to
do an emergency C-section.

00:06:29.040 --> 00:06:31.873
He came out four pounds, eight ounces.

00:06:41.660 --> 00:06:42.950
Basically, he couldn't come home

00:06:42.950 --> 00:06:45.640
the day that I left from the hospital.

00:06:45.640 --> 00:06:47.953
He had to stay in there
for two extra months.

00:06:54.870 --> 00:06:56.750
- [Mark] You still have your kids?

00:06:56.750 --> 00:06:57.583
You do.

00:06:57.583 --> 00:06:59.080
You're raising them?

00:06:59.080 --> 00:06:59.913
Good for you.

00:07:14.710 --> 00:07:18.293
(Juicy weeps and sniffles)

00:07:25.600 --> 00:07:28.002
Tell me about your kids.

00:07:28.002 --> 00:07:30.630
(sirens blaring)

00:07:30.630 --> 00:07:34.690
- (sighs) Well, my daughter's
gonna be 17 next year.

00:07:34.690 --> 00:07:36.744
She's 16 right now.

00:07:36.744 --> 00:07:39.530
(sniffles and clear's throat)

00:07:39.530 --> 00:07:40.443
My son is 14.

00:07:46.923 --> 00:07:48.630
(sniffles)

00:07:48.630 --> 00:07:50.690
- [Mark] They good kids?

00:07:50.690 --> 00:07:51.523
- Very smart.

00:07:57.103 --> 00:08:00.033
I just don't want my
daughter to be like me.

00:08:03.432 --> 00:08:05.682
(sniffles)

00:08:06.535 --> 00:08:08.700
- [Mark] You think there's a chance of her

00:08:08.700 --> 00:08:09.750
doing the same thing?

00:08:11.243 --> 00:08:12.326
- I hope not.

00:08:18.694 --> 00:08:21.777
(weeps and sniffles)

00:08:36.671 --> 00:08:38.921
(sniffles)

00:08:42.444 --> 00:08:45.903
I don't want her to follow in
the same footsteps that I did.

00:08:48.738 --> 00:08:51.321
(sighs deeply)

00:08:53.440 --> 00:08:56.080
- [Mark] Does she know
what you do for work?

00:08:56.080 --> 00:08:58.500
- [Juicy Fruit] I don't lie
to my kids about anything.

00:08:58.500 --> 00:09:00.750
I let 'em know the truth about everything.

00:09:06.370 --> 00:09:09.120
(Juicy whimpers)

00:09:14.269 --> 00:09:16.519
(sniffles)

00:09:21.780 --> 00:09:23.240
I love my kids to death.

00:09:23.240 --> 00:09:24.720
I would do anything for them.

00:09:31.122 --> 00:09:33.760
- [Mark] And you're still working today?

00:09:33.760 --> 00:09:36.160
Do you make enough money
to support your family?

00:09:37.310 --> 00:09:38.460
- [Juicy Fruit] Almost.

00:09:47.210 --> 00:09:50.050
- [Mark] It's still a very
dangerous way to make a living.

00:09:50.050 --> 00:09:52.450
You have kids to come home to and support.

00:09:52.450 --> 00:09:55.741
- [Juicy Fruit] Yeah, 'cause
every time I go out there

00:09:55.741 --> 00:09:58.507
I'm thinking, "Am I gonna make
it back to my kids or not?"

00:10:05.762 --> 00:10:08.012
(sniffles)

00:10:17.220 --> 00:10:20.020
- [Mark] Tell me about the
guys that are your customers.

00:10:21.180 --> 00:10:23.833
- Oh, Lord. (chuckles)

00:10:30.830 --> 00:10:34.430
You have to deal with these
guys, different attitudes.

00:10:34.430 --> 00:10:36.730
Yeah, some of them might
be nice but very few.

00:10:41.400 --> 00:10:45.440
You have some that'll pretend to be nice.

00:10:45.440 --> 00:10:48.900
How you say, once you finish
handling whatever business

00:10:48.900 --> 00:10:51.050
you have to handle with them, it's like,

00:10:51.050 --> 00:10:52.160
they want to take the money back

00:10:52.160 --> 00:10:53.610
or they want half of it back.

00:10:53.610 --> 00:10:54.677
I'm like, "What?"

00:11:00.670 --> 00:11:02.720
I've had to stab a guy in the leg before.

00:11:10.290 --> 00:11:11.870
Because the dude basically

00:11:11.870 --> 00:11:15.430
tried to hold me down afterwards and

00:11:18.630 --> 00:11:20.530
thought he's gonna get his money back.

00:11:21.550 --> 00:11:23.550
He thought he was gonna put hands on me.

00:11:25.500 --> 00:11:27.540
I've been dragged by a car before

00:11:29.260 --> 00:11:30.883
on my stomach, a whole block.

00:11:37.370 --> 00:11:40.880
Just the beginning of this
year, I've been hit by a car

00:11:40.880 --> 00:11:41.830
and I've been shot.

00:11:46.698 --> 00:11:48.948
(sniffles)

00:11:52.610 --> 00:11:56.390
But at the end of the day,
if I don't make money,

00:11:56.390 --> 00:11:58.153
can't support me and my kids.

00:12:01.530 --> 00:12:03.620
At the end of the day, I
still have to go out there

00:12:03.620 --> 00:12:04.870
and do what I have to do.

00:12:11.440 --> 00:12:13.980
So it's like, you can't
let stuff scare you

00:12:13.980 --> 00:12:15.080
when you're out there.

00:12:17.500 --> 00:12:19.500
Because should you let it scare you,

00:12:19.500 --> 00:12:20.650
how can you make money?

00:12:22.280 --> 00:12:24.293
And because I have my kids to support,

00:12:28.818 --> 00:12:30.273
I have to do what I have to do.

00:12:35.120 --> 00:12:36.560
- [Mark] Are you using drugs.

00:12:36.560 --> 00:12:37.453
- I smoke weed.

00:12:42.240 --> 00:12:44.570
- [Mark] How do you
think living this life,

00:12:44.570 --> 00:12:47.170
working the streets has
changed you all these years?

00:12:49.760 --> 00:12:53.090
- Um, think it's changed me a lot.

00:12:57.587 --> 00:12:59.837
(sniffles)

00:13:04.916 --> 00:13:05.749
Thank you.

00:13:18.055 --> 00:13:21.855
- [Mark] How do you
think it's changed you?

00:13:21.855 --> 00:13:24.050
- I think it's changed me a lot because

00:13:27.150 --> 00:13:30.170
basically if everything
that had happened to me

00:13:30.170 --> 00:13:31.403
wouldn't have happened to me,

00:13:31.403 --> 00:13:33.610
I wouldn't be the person I am today also

00:13:35.780 --> 00:13:37.690
'cause I've gained a lot of street smarts.

00:13:37.690 --> 00:13:41.270
Not only do I have book smarts,
I have street smarts too.

00:13:41.270 --> 00:13:43.823
So made me a lot smarter,

00:13:45.280 --> 00:13:47.643
basically being in the streets.

00:13:49.240 --> 00:13:53.640
Because like, a lot of times
I know what to look for

00:13:53.640 --> 00:13:55.130
before I get in the car.

00:13:55.130 --> 00:13:56.080
- [Mark] You use your intuition?

00:13:56.080 --> 00:13:58.740
- Exactly, my first mind so.

00:13:58.740 --> 00:14:01.020
- [Mark] What kind of
stuff do you shy away from?

00:14:01.020 --> 00:14:04.763
- Too fidgety, too anxious
for me to get in the car,

00:14:06.120 --> 00:14:08.763
too like, flashy of money too much.

00:14:09.994 --> 00:14:12.723
That's bell ringers right there.

00:14:13.650 --> 00:14:15.930
'Cause that's like, nine times out of 10,

00:14:15.930 --> 00:14:17.790
they gonna wanna pull into an alley

00:14:19.390 --> 00:14:22.100
or something like that or
in front of somewhere dark

00:14:22.100 --> 00:14:25.090
where they can't nobody
see in the car or anything.

00:14:25.090 --> 00:14:27.290
And 9 times out of 10, they gon' rape you

00:14:27.290 --> 00:14:28.240
or try to kill you.

00:14:34.800 --> 00:14:37.103
I've been kidnapped by pimps.

00:14:39.300 --> 00:14:42.280
I've been kidnapped by a pimp before,

00:14:42.280 --> 00:14:44.123
to where my kids thought I was dead.

00:14:50.030 --> 00:14:51.763
They had me in a cage.

00:14:53.760 --> 00:14:55.203
They fed me like a animal.

00:15:12.440 --> 00:15:14.390
They had a shark collar around my neck.

00:15:20.293 --> 00:15:22.193
- [Mark] How do you think girls get so

00:15:23.370 --> 00:15:26.020
brainwashed to work with a pimp?

00:15:26.020 --> 00:15:28.960
- Because they believe
that these dudes love them

00:15:28.960 --> 00:15:32.210
but in all honestly, these dudes,

00:15:32.210 --> 00:15:33.700
they don't really love them.

00:15:33.700 --> 00:15:35.750
They love the money that they get them.

00:15:39.840 --> 00:15:40.673
How you say?...

00:15:40.673 --> 00:15:45.360
These guys out here, they
learn how to finesse a female.

00:15:45.360 --> 00:15:47.210
Tell a female what she wants to hear.

00:15:48.670 --> 00:15:50.320
And whatever that he
thinks she wants to hear,

00:15:50.320 --> 00:15:51.560
that's what he's gonna tell her.

00:15:51.560 --> 00:15:52.610
Whatever sounds good.

00:15:56.830 --> 00:15:59.890
They'll play with your
emotions and your feelings

00:15:59.890 --> 00:16:01.440
so they can get what they want.

00:16:02.510 --> 00:16:04.633
And then when their use of you is over,

00:16:07.131 --> 00:16:09.350
Hey, they go to the next one.

00:16:09.350 --> 00:16:11.450
And they'll still try to string you along.

00:16:25.310 --> 00:16:26.890
- [Mark] What advice would
you give to a young girl

00:16:26.890 --> 00:16:28.893
who's considering doing this kind of work?

00:16:31.090 --> 00:16:33.463
- Don't do it, stay in school.

00:16:36.290 --> 00:16:39.063
You know, get good
grades, don't ditch class.

00:16:41.180 --> 00:16:43.170
Just listen to your parents

00:16:47.740 --> 00:16:51.423
and don't do drugs at all, period.

00:16:52.440 --> 00:16:53.463
Not even weed.

00:16:58.090 --> 00:16:59.900
- [Mark] What's the most
important lesson you've learned

00:16:59.900 --> 00:17:01.300
in your years of doing this?

00:17:04.960 --> 00:17:06.343
- Be careful who you trust.

00:17:13.421 --> 00:17:15.754
You have to be very careful.

00:17:20.993 --> 00:17:22.984
(sniffles)

00:17:22.984 --> 00:17:24.440
- [Mark] You think this kind of work

00:17:24.440 --> 00:17:26.163
has changed the way you view men?

00:17:27.660 --> 00:17:28.493
- Yeah.

00:17:30.790 --> 00:17:31.840
- [Mark] In what way?

00:17:34.100 --> 00:17:36.210
- To where I don't even...

00:17:43.860 --> 00:17:46.320
I'm bisexual. I used to be gay.

00:17:46.320 --> 00:17:48.920
I used to just do this out
here like, for the money.

00:17:50.020 --> 00:17:51.650
But it's like dudes, it's like,

00:17:51.650 --> 00:17:53.290
I don't even like either now.

00:17:53.290 --> 00:17:56.183
And I'm just like, just
everybody leave me alone.

00:17:58.010 --> 00:18:01.190
It's like, this shit that
made me hate people so bad.

00:18:01.190 --> 00:18:02.433
It's like, damn.

00:18:12.600 --> 00:18:13.980
The only reason I'm still living

00:18:13.980 --> 00:18:17.103
and going through life
is because of my kids.

00:18:18.270 --> 00:18:20.873
They give me a reason to
wake up in the morning.

00:18:31.089 --> 00:18:33.256
(weeping)

00:18:39.291 --> 00:18:41.541
(sniffles)

00:18:47.699 --> 00:18:50.730
(sniffles)

00:18:50.730 --> 00:18:53.430
My kid's name is Lynnita Smith

00:18:53.430 --> 00:18:55.133
and my son name is Jesse.

00:18:56.740 --> 00:18:57.593
Jesse Lynn.

00:18:59.381 --> 00:19:02.464
(sniffles and sighs)

00:19:03.550 --> 00:19:05.450
- [Mark] You're proud of your kids?

00:19:05.450 --> 00:19:06.283
- Hmm?

00:19:06.283 --> 00:19:07.582
- [Mark] You're proud of your kids?

00:19:07.582 --> 00:19:08.713
- I'm very proud.

00:19:10.760 --> 00:19:12.613
- [Mark] You should be proud
of yourself too though.

00:19:16.731 --> 00:19:17.564
(sniffles)

00:19:17.564 --> 00:19:18.397
- I do the best I can.

00:19:20.170 --> 00:19:21.003
- [Mark] You're trying to protect them

00:19:21.003 --> 00:19:24.917
from the same thing you went through.

00:19:24.917 --> 00:19:26.017
You never had parents.

00:19:27.256 --> 00:19:30.839
(Juicy weeps and sniffles)

00:19:39.413 --> 00:19:41.380
- [Mark] Have you ever been in love?

00:19:41.380 --> 00:19:42.266
(sniffles)

00:19:42.266 --> 00:19:46.030
- (chuckles) Hell no.

00:19:46.030 --> 00:19:48.772
Not what I thought was love... (chuckles)

00:19:48.772 --> 00:19:49.605
What I thought was love.

00:19:54.450 --> 00:19:55.970
- [Mark] Do you think love exists?

00:19:55.970 --> 00:19:57.060
- Huh?

00:19:57.060 --> 00:19:58.760
- [Mark] Do you think love exists?

00:20:01.230 --> 00:20:02.063
True love.

00:20:05.112 --> 00:20:06.113
- I really don't.

00:20:10.760 --> 00:20:12.510
Because anybody can say I love you.

00:20:15.907 --> 00:20:19.653
What really matters is,
I'll tell you like this;

00:20:21.950 --> 00:20:23.043
hit rock bottom.

00:20:24.500 --> 00:20:25.860
When you hit rock bottom,

00:20:25.860 --> 00:20:27.710
then you'll see who really loves you.

00:20:28.640 --> 00:20:30.040
You never know who really loves you

00:20:30.040 --> 00:20:31.600
or who's really there for you

00:20:32.490 --> 00:20:34.153
until you really need somebody.

00:20:53.407 --> 00:20:54.240
(sniffles)

00:20:54.240 --> 00:20:55.073
- [Mark] All right, Juicy Fruit.

00:20:55.073 --> 00:20:57.730
Thank you so much for sharing your story.

00:20:57.730 --> 00:21:01.080
- [Juicy Fruit] Thank you.

00:21:01.080 --> 00:21:01.913
(sniffles)

00:21:01.913 --> 00:21:03.720
- [Mark] I'm gonna take care of you.

00:21:03.720 --> 00:21:05.553
You'll make some nice money this weekend.

